# Ogeemo Website — Image Placeholder Catalog

**Last updated:** August 13, 2026  
**Purpose:** Complete inventory of all `ImagePlaceholder` IDs used across the Ogeemo website. Use this as a checklist when uploading images via the admin interface (footer → Admin Login → Manage Site Images).

---

## How It Works

The Ogeemo website uses a CMS-like image system:
1. Each `ImagePlaceholder` component has a unique `id` (e.g., `about-dan`)
2. Images are uploaded to Firestore and linked by ID
3. When a page loads, the component fetches the image from Firestore by ID
4. If no image is set, a placeholder with "No image set for '[id]'" is displayed
5. Authenticated admins can hover over any placeholder and click the edit button to upload or select an image

**To upload images:** Log in via the footer "Admin Login" link, then visit `/image-manager` or hover over any placeholder on the site and click the edit (pencil) button.

